1
00:00:07,581 --> 00:00:10,476
A sound has just stopped. A day is over.

2
00:00:10,556 --> 00:00:13,887
Someone you loved has died.
And with it comes a picture.

3
00:00:13,967 --> 00:00:17,967
Something was fully there, and now
there is a blank where it stood.

4
00:00:18,782 --> 00:00:23,974
Here is the question. If nothing lasts for
ever, is everything wiped out in the end?

5
00:00:24,054 --> 00:00:27,443
Is that the honest view, the
one that gives up clinging?

6
00:00:28,253 --> 00:00:33,367
This is After Anatta: notes by
John Tan, known as Thusness.

7
00:00:34,171 --> 00:00:39,010
Annihilation sounds like the opposite
of holding on to things. It is not.

8
00:00:39,090 --> 00:00:42,787
It holds on to the same
thing eternalism holds on to,

9
00:00:42,867 --> 00:00:46,283
and only tells a different
story about what happens to it.

10
00:00:47,101 --> 00:00:49,330
The reason fits in one line.

11
00:00:49,410 --> 00:00:53,859
Something can be annihilated only if
it was there from its own side first.

12
00:00:54,665 --> 00:00:59,698
To say, it is gone, cut off, now
nothing, you first need an "it".

13
00:00:59,868 --> 00:01:03,430
A thing that stood on its
own, and is now wiped out.

14
00:01:03,510 --> 00:01:07,710
So annihilation keeps the very
thing that eternalism keeps.

15
00:01:07,790 --> 00:01:10,250
Eternalism says the thing stays.

16
00:01:10,330 --> 00:01:13,199
Annihilation says the thing is destroyed.

17
00:01:13,279 --> 00:01:16,500
Both start from a thing
with a being of its own.

18
00:01:16,580 --> 00:01:19,494
They differ only in what
they say happens to it.

19
00:01:20,301 --> 00:01:23,323
Nāgārjuna puts the two side by side.

20
00:01:23,453 --> 00:01:26,095
"It is" is the grasping of permanence.

21
00:01:26,225 --> 00:01:29,066
"It is not" is the view of annihilation.

22
00:01:29,146 --> 00:01:32,136
So the wise should not take
their stand on existence,

23
00:01:32,216 --> 00:01:33,921
or on non-existence.

24
00:01:34,729 --> 00:01:37,135
And he shows where
annihilation comes from.

25
00:01:37,215 --> 00:01:42,352
What exists by its own nature does not
cease to exist: that is permanence.

26
00:01:42,432 --> 00:01:45,641
It existed before, and does not exist now:

27
00:01:45,721 --> 00:01:47,330
that brings annihilation.

28
00:01:48,162 --> 00:01:50,840
The word that gives it away is "before".

29
00:01:50,920 --> 00:01:55,596
The thing is pictured as fully there,
with its own nature, and then gone.

30
00:01:55,676 --> 00:01:59,975
A thing with its own nature falls
into a nothing that is just as solid.

31
00:02:00,777 --> 00:02:02,762
Look closely at "it is not".

32
00:02:02,842 --> 00:02:06,811
Non-existence is not a second
fact, standing on its own.

33
00:02:06,891 --> 00:02:08,822
It is borrowed from existence.

34
00:02:08,902 --> 00:02:12,898
Nāgārjuna says, if an existing
thing is not established,

35
00:02:12,978 --> 00:02:16,254
a non-existing thing is
not established either.

36
00:02:16,334 --> 00:02:20,484
For people call the change of an
existing thing its non-existence.

37
00:02:21,369 --> 00:02:24,753
"Gone" only means something
as the going of something.

38
00:02:24,833 --> 00:02:29,617
Take away the self-standing thing, and the
self-standing nothing has nothing to be

39
00:02:29,697 --> 00:02:31,062
the absence of.

40
00:02:31,878 --> 00:02:35,467
This is why the two extremes
cannot be fought one at a time.

41
00:02:35,547 --> 00:02:38,497
Refute eternalism while keeping the thing,

42
00:02:38,577 --> 00:02:40,643
and you land in annihilation.

43
00:02:40,723 --> 00:02:46,024
Whoever accepts that things truly exist
from their own side falls into permanence,

44
00:02:46,104 --> 00:02:47,763
or into annihilation.

45
00:02:47,843 --> 00:02:51,377
Such a thing would have to
last for ever, or be cut off.

46
00:02:51,457 --> 00:02:53,198
There is no third way for it.

47
00:02:53,278 --> 00:02:57,401
The fork opens only for a thing
that exists from its own side.

48
00:02:58,221 --> 00:03:01,850
Now look with dependency, and
start where it can be felt.

49
00:03:01,930 --> 00:03:07,930
Listen to a sound nearby, a fan, a
car, a voice. Wait for it to stop.

50
00:03:09,025 --> 00:03:13,918
When it stops, where did it go? Not
back into the fan. Not into the air.

51
00:03:13,998 --> 00:03:16,812
Not into your ear. It did not go anywhere.

52
00:03:16,892 --> 00:03:19,719
The sound was never found
apart from the source,

53
00:03:19,799 --> 00:03:23,727
the air, the ear and the
attention coming together.

54
00:03:23,807 --> 00:03:26,105
When they part, there is no sound.

55
00:03:26,185 --> 00:03:28,840
Nothing that stood on its
own has been destroyed.

56
00:03:29,645 --> 00:03:31,698
A candle flame is the same.

57
00:03:31,778 --> 00:03:36,671
It goes out when the wick, the wax
and the air no longer come together.

58
00:03:36,751 --> 00:03:39,202
There never was a flame
apart from the burning.

59
00:03:40,030 --> 00:03:43,768
So an ending is not the loss of
something that stood by itself.

60
00:03:43,848 --> 00:03:48,687
It is conditions parting, just as the
arising was conditions coming together.

61
00:03:48,767 --> 00:03:52,536
Nothing self-standing comes,
so nothing self-standing goes.

62
00:03:53,341 --> 00:03:56,576
That is why the homage of the
Middle Way reads them together.

63
00:03:56,656 --> 00:04:00,557
Without ceasing, without
arising, without annihilation,

64
00:04:00,637 --> 00:04:04,511
without permanence, not
one thing and not many,

65
00:04:04,591 --> 00:04:09,225
without coming and without going: so
the fully awakened one taught dependent

66
00:04:09,305 --> 00:04:10,505
arising.

67
00:04:11,081 --> 00:04:15,566
Remove inherent existence, and
both extremes fall at once.

68
00:04:15,646 --> 00:04:18,460
Not because a middle object
is found between them,

69
00:04:18,540 --> 00:04:22,255
but because the object they
were both about is never found.

70
00:04:23,061 --> 00:04:25,662
None of this denies
that the sound stopped.

71
00:04:25,832 --> 00:04:31,106
"The sound stopped" is true, said the way
the world says it. The room is quiet now.

72
00:04:31,186 --> 00:04:35,073
That quiet is validly functioning:
you can hear the next thing.

73
00:04:35,153 --> 00:04:38,130
What is denied is a sound
with its own nature,

74
00:04:38,210 --> 00:04:41,001
falling into a nothing
with its own nature.

75
00:04:41,809 --> 00:04:44,473
Annihilation rarely announces itself.

76
00:04:44,553 --> 00:04:46,502
It hides in three places.

77
00:04:47,363 --> 00:04:48,642
First, at death.

78
00:04:48,722 --> 00:04:53,859
The fear, I will be wiped out, assumes
an I that was there from its own side.

79
00:04:53,939 --> 00:04:56,916
The search never finds
that I, in the body,

80
00:04:56,996 --> 00:04:59,294
in the mind, or apart from them.

81
00:04:59,374 --> 00:05:01,780
So nothing of that kind can be wiped out.

82
00:05:01,860 --> 00:05:05,856
Seeing, hearing and thinking
were never carried by a someone,

83
00:05:05,936 --> 00:05:09,226
and so they are not cut off
when a someone is not found.

84
00:05:09,306 --> 00:05:13,361
The flow of conditions goes
on, neither carried nor cut.

85
00:05:14,169 --> 00:05:16,466
Second, in emptiness itself.

86
00:05:16,546 --> 00:05:19,700
Everything is empty, so nothing exists.

87
00:05:19,780 --> 00:05:23,817
That reads emptiness as the destruction
of things that were there from their own

88
00:05:23,897 --> 00:05:27,268
side. It is annihilation
dressed as insight.

89
00:05:27,348 --> 00:05:30,651
Emptiness never removes
anything that was there.

90
00:05:30,731 --> 00:05:33,437
It shows that nothing was
ever there in that way.

91
00:05:33,517 --> 00:05:36,412
Nāgārjuna warns about exactly this.

92
00:05:36,492 --> 00:05:39,727
Emptiness wrongly seen
ruins the slow-witted,

93
00:05:39,807 --> 00:05:44,442
like a snake grasped the wrong
way, or a spell cast the wrong way.

94
00:05:44,522 --> 00:05:49,075
The faults charged against emptiness are
faults of the nothingness it was mistaken

95
00:05:49,155 --> 00:05:50,355
for.

96
00:05:50,851 --> 00:05:52,578
Third, in practice.

97
00:05:52,658 --> 00:05:56,491
After awakening, causes
and ethics no longer apply.

98
00:05:56,571 --> 00:05:58,217
That makes the same mistake.

99
00:05:58,297 --> 00:06:02,497
It treats insight as the cutting
off of conditions that once held.

100
00:06:02,577 --> 00:06:04,181
But conditions still work.

101
00:06:04,261 --> 00:06:07,728
An unkind word still
hurts. Care still heals.

102
00:06:07,808 --> 00:06:10,486
Only the inherent version
of them was never there.

103
00:06:10,566 --> 00:06:14,403
Seeing that does not cancel what
works. It is what lets it work.

104
00:06:15,209 --> 00:06:17,955
Try it now. Think of
something that has ended.

105
00:06:18,035 --> 00:06:20,509
A sound, a day, a friendship.

106
00:06:20,589 --> 00:06:23,131
Notice the picture that
comes with "it is gone".

107
00:06:23,211 --> 00:06:27,293
A thing that was fully there, and
is now a blank where it stood.

108
00:06:28,101 --> 00:06:30,303
Now look for that thing
at the time it was there.

109
00:06:30,383 --> 00:06:32,722
Was the sound found apart from the source,

110
00:06:32,802 --> 00:06:34,583
the air and the hearing?

111
00:06:34,663 --> 00:06:38,306
Was the day found apart from the
light, the turning of the earth,

112
00:06:38,386 --> 00:06:39,586
and the counting?

113
00:06:40,249 --> 00:06:42,859
If it was never found standing by itself,

114
00:06:42,939 --> 00:06:45,019
what is it that has been annihilated?

115
00:06:45,099 --> 00:06:46,772
The ending is still an ending.

116
00:06:46,852 --> 00:06:50,730
It is just not the destruction of
anything that stood on its own.

117
00:06:51,533 --> 00:06:55,026
In brief. Eternalism says the thing stays.

118
00:06:55,106 --> 00:06:57,974
Annihilation says the thing is destroyed.

119
00:06:58,054 --> 00:07:00,542
Both assume a thing with its own nature.

120
00:07:00,622 --> 00:07:03,885
Seen with dependency,
nothing self-standing comes,

121
00:07:03,965 --> 00:07:06,090
and nothing self-standing goes.

122
00:07:06,883 --> 00:07:10,580
Annihilation is the inherent
view looking backwards.

123
00:07:10,660 --> 00:07:15,068
It needs something to have been there
from its own side, in order to lose it.

124
00:07:15,877 --> 00:07:18,840
This is one point, seen from three sides.

125
00:07:18,920 --> 00:07:22,998
Neither Carried Nor Cut looks
at it in your own six streams,

126
00:07:23,078 --> 00:07:27,876
from moment to moment. One Flame Lights
Another looks at it from life to life.

127
00:07:27,956 --> 00:07:30,158
Here it is seen from
the side of the ending.

128
00:07:30,238 --> 00:07:34,669
Each time the same thing falls away:
something there from its own side,

129
00:07:34,749 --> 00:07:37,323
to be carried, or to be cut off.

